# Zustand stores

Canonical example: @app/stores/blockedUsers.ts

## Shape

```ts
const initialState = { /* flat state */ }

interface FeatureState {
  // flat state fields
  actions: {
    // all mutations here
  }
}

export const useFeatureStore = create<FeatureState>()((set) => ({
  ...initialState,
  actions: { /* stable object */ },
}))
```

- One small store per domain/feature. No giant app store.
- Flat state + single `actions` object (stable reference).
- Immutable updates. Prefer arrays/`filter`/`spread` over `delete`.
- Client UI state only. Server data stays in React Query.

## Consuming

```ts
// ✅ select specific state
const value = useFeatureStore((s) => s.value)
const actions = useFeatureStore((s) => s.actions)

// ❌ never
const store = useFeatureStore()
```

- Prefer multiple selectors over shallow.
- Use `shallow` from `zustand/shallow` only for: 3+ related primitives in one object, arrays of primitives for lists, or prop-spread objects of primitives.
- Do not use shallow for a single value, nested objects, or `state.actions`.

## File header

New/updated stores keep the store-rules comment block from @app/stores/blockedUsers.ts (selectors, stable actions, shallow when/don't).
